From 61324df1b668d8634e39edc83cf210837a17cc4d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 14:29:51 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 207/209] fix(area): spline evaluation with fewer than three
 points

Create -> Area -> Spline crashed Sandbox on the second click. Stack overflow
from unbounded recursion, and the exact line is the arc-length loop inside
CSplineShapeComponent::GetCache():

    for (int s = 0; s < segmentCount; ++s)
    {
        int i0, i1;
        SegmentPoints(s, i0, i1);      // <- this

f75669e0 changed SegmentPoints() to read GetCache().localPos.size(), which it
has to: with smoothing on, the evaluation polygon is no longer the authored
point list. But GetCache() is the function that loop is inside, still building,
with m_cache.bValid still false - so SegmentPoints() called GetCache(), which
started another build, which called SegmentPoints() again, until the stack ran
out. It could only fire once there was at least one segment, i.e. from the
second point onwards, which is exactly when the crash appeared. One point, the
state the first click leaves behind, has segmentCount 0 and never enters the
loop.

The fix is one rule and one line: nothing inside a cache build may read the
cache, so the segment's two end indices are computed in place from the local
count. A re-entry guard (m_bBuildingCache) is added on top, because half the
evaluation helpers legitimately read the cache and this is easy to break again;
if it ever is, the caller gets the half-built cache for one frame instead of a
stack overflow.

The degenerate cases the create tool walks through are now explicit rather than
implied. SegmentPos() with fewer than two evaluation points answers the single
point (or the origin with none) instead of relying on GetSegmentCount(), and
SegmentTangent() answers zero rather than normalising nothing - which is what
keeps NaN out of every frame built downstream. The rest of the audit came back
clean: SubdivideInterpolating clamps its outer stencil indices for an open
polygon (max(e-1,0) / min(e+2,count-1)) and is skipped entirely at the default
0 iterations, MakeSeedNormal answers a fixed perpendicular for a zero tangent
rather than normalising it, PropagateNormal guards both reflection divisors, and
PosByDistance is a linear scan over a table that is empty when there are no
segments.

Added `area_SplineSelfTest`, a console command that walks the maths through the
shapes a half-drawn spline produces - 1 point, 2 coincident points, 2 points,
3 collinear, 3 vertical, 3 general - open and closed, 0 to 2 smoothing passes,
both frame modes, and reports the first non-finite position, tangent, handle,
length or normal. It exercises SplineMath directly rather than a live component,
because the states that matter are the ones with no entity yet.

